{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Before all his brethren.</b> They are Zimran and Jokshan." "<b> Fell.</b> His portion or his lot; or that most of Ishmael's sons travel from place to place, in the sense of \"to the Chaldeans you are falling\" (Jeremiah 37:13). And this is somewhat far-fetched, because his brethren are to the east, and Egypt and Assyria are to the west of the land of Israel. And it is possible that the verse spoke of Ishmael, that he died during the lifetime of his brethren, one who fell, for we do not know the cause of his death:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:45.447945718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}